 },
 "_comment": "Curated description of every mirrored SDRBench dataset. Each variant (keyed by its Python API name; the first is the default) names its Hugging Face 'folder', its Globus 'archive' (relative to globus_base) and optionally 'select' / 'exclude', globs choosing which of the archive's files it uses. 'rules' map file globs (first match wins) to a numpy dtype and a C-order shape (slowest first; \"1d\" = flat); 'pattern' is a regex on the file path inside the folder whose groups fill the 'var' (physical variable) and 'step' (time step / slab) templates; 'components' splits axis 0 of each file into one field per listed variable (zero-copy views). A rule with dtype null marks a non-array file. 'view_of' + 'transpose' define a derived layout computed on load. 'description' is science prose only: counts, shapes and names are generated. Every non-text file must match a rule with a matching size, or the catalog build fails.",
 "datasets": {
  "cesm-atm": {
   "title": "CESM-ATM",
   "source": "Mark Taylor (SNL)",
